(954323, 111795, 23956, '<td valign="top">Very nice as a vertical shot. I''m not lowering my rating of this photograph for the orientation, since it doesn''t really change the image at all, but I don''t think that the horizontal rotation works at all here. Unless she''s laying on black sheets, this doesn''t make sense. Otherwise, I love the graininess, the focus control, the tones... it''s a lovely shot.</td>', 'Very nice as a vertical shot. I''m not lowering my rating of this photograph for the orientation, since it doesn''t really change the image at all, but I don''t think that the horizontal rotation works at all here. Unless she''s laying on black sheets, this doesn''t make sense. Otherwise, I love the graininess, the focus control, the tones... it''s a lovely shot.', '2004-10-11 13:15:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(954330, 110172, 23956, '<td valign="top">The image on the far left doesn''t look like the same person as the others, because we can''t see her hair in the flashes on the right, and because the expression is so different. The lighting is also not as drastic (light source farther away?) I''d actually crop out the left third of this image, or just edit out that last personality.</td>', 'The image on the far left doesn''t look like the same person as the others, because we can''t see her hair in the flashes on the right, and because the expression is so different. The lighting is also not as drastic (light source farther away?) I''d actually crop out the left third of this image, or just edit out that last personality.', '2004-10-11 13:19:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(954345, 111511, 23956, '<td valign="top">Is that an animal bone? And is an opposable thumb really what sets this person apart from the rest of humanity? Well photographed, but this shot doesn''t make sense without an explanation.</td>', 'Is that an animal bone? And is an opposable thumb really what sets this person apart from the rest of humanity? Well photographed, but this shot doesn''t make sense without an explanation.', '2004-10-11 13:25:48.000000', NULL, 1),
