(963682, 111481, 9821, '<td valign="top">great job as usual :)</td>', 'great job as usual :)', '2004-10-18 10:21:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(963688, 111848, 18028, '<td valign="top">Congrads dude!  awsome placing...and fab shot.</td>', 'Congrads dude!  awsome placing...and fab shot.', '2004-10-18 10:46:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(963689, 111848, 18028, '<td valign="top">how and why would someone give a shot like this a 1 is beyong me.</td>', 'how and why would someone give a shot like this a 1 is beyong me.', '2004-10-18 10:47:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(963690, 111547, 1368, '<td valign="top">Finally a blue for you! Congrats on this beautiful shot And a great score!</td>', 'Finally a blue for you! Congrats on this beautiful shot And a great score!', '2004-10-18 10:48:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(963695, 111547, 22748, '<td valign="top">You know you have created yourself a style all your own when you can identify the photographer during the challenge simply from the photograph''s feel and texture. Like Ansel Adams'' images, librodo''s images are that distinctive.<br/> <br/>What lens did you use for this shot? Did you shoot RAW? What kind of post processing? Did you use a reflector or is it all just window light? Thanks!<br/> <br/>(wow! no 1 votes!)</td>', 'You know you have created yourself a style all your own when you can identify the photographer during the challenge simply from the photograph''s feel and texture. Like Ansel Adams'' images, librodo''s images are that distinctive. What lens did you use for this shot? Did you shoot RAW? What kind of post processing? Did you use a reflector or is it all just window light? Thanks! (wow! no 1 votes!)', '2004-10-18 10:57:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(963759, 111473, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congrats John... beautiful shot.  And congrats to your wife for being so dedicated to her gorgeous figure!  :o)</td>', 'Congrats John... beautiful shot.  And congrats to your wife for being so dedicated to her gorgeous figure!  :o)', '2004-10-18 12:18:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(963760, 111481, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Jacko... this is such a sweet photo, and regardless of the ribbon, you''ll look back on it for years and smile!  :o)</td>', 'Congratulations, Jacko... this is such a sweet photo, and regardless of the ribbon, you''ll look back on it for years and smile!  :o)', '2004-10-18 12:19:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(963761, 111728, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your 6th place finish, Brian!  This is such a beautiful shot...but of course, it has to be with Gracie as your model!  :o)</td>', 'Congratulations on your 6th place finish, Brian!  This is such a beautiful shot...but of course, it has to be with Gracie as your model!  :o)', '2004-10-18 12:21:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(963763, 111809, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congrats Denis... this is an excellent image that well deserves it''s top ten finish!  :o)</td>', 'Congrats Denis... this is an excellent image that well deserves it''s top ten finish!  :o)', '2004-10-18 12:21:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(963764, 111848, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  This is one of my favorites from the challenge...congrats on the top ten finish!  :o)</td>', 'Congrats!  This is one of my favorites from the challenge...congrats on the top ten finish!  :o)', '2004-10-18 12:22:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(963767, 111547, 18349, '<td valign="top">What else can I add?  This is just stunning, as per your usual... Congrats Manny on the blue.  Beautiful!  :o)</td>', 'What else can I add?  This is just stunning, as per your usual... Congrats Manny on the blue.  Beautiful!  :o)', '2004-10-18 12:24:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(963779, 111511, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hlswilson:</b></div><hr/><i> Returning for comments: I struggled with this one. After looking at this photo for quite a while, and finally recognizing that the model was holding a bone, I realized that you were tring to say that a human being''s defining feature is the opposable thumb. What would have improved this photo greatly for me would have been to have a more recognizable bone - like one of those big knuckle bones that you can purchase for dogs in pet stores. Also, I know that it might be cliche'' but the photo would make more sense to me if a big, burly, hairy, caveman like guy were holding the bone. This small, delicate hand made it difficult for me to understand what you were trying to convey. Lastly, I would have used a little more light to help dispell some of the shadow under the fingers. Your idea was excellent, but refining the execution would make this a much stronger shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for the comments! I looked for a bigger bone but couldn''t find one in time ... that''s a turkey drumstick. Isaac is kind of hairy for his age (like his dad!), but it doesn''t show that well here : )<br/>I thought about getting a gorilla hand (Halloween shops are open) but didn''t get around to it in time.<br/> <br/>Next time I try a shot like this I''ll try to put a white sheet on the ground to reflect some sunlight up onto the underside of the hand.</td>', 'Originally posted by hlswilson: Returning for comments: I struggled with this one. After looking at this photo for quite a while, and finally recognizing that the model was holding a bone, I realized that you were tring to say that a human being''s defining feature is the opposable thumb. What would have improved this photo greatly for me would have been to have a more recognizable bone - like one of those big knuckle bones that you can purchase for dogs in pet stores. Also, I know that it might be cliche'' but the photo would make more sense to me if a big, burly, hairy, caveman like guy were holding the bone. This small, delicate hand made it difficult for me to understand what you were trying to convey. Lastly, I would have used a little more light to help dispell some of the shadow under the fingers. Your idea was excellent, but refining the execution would make this a much stronger shot.  Thanks for the comments! I looked for a bigger bone but couldn''t find one in time ... that''s a turkey drumstick. Isaac is kind of hairy for his age (like his dad!), but it doesn''t show that well here : )I thought about getting a gorilla hand (Halloween shops are open) but didn''t get around to it in time. Next time I try a shot like this I''ll try to put a white sheet on the ground to reflect some sunlight up onto the underside of the hand.', '2004-10-18 12:37:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(963793, 111876, 1368, '<td valign="top">Congrats on 5th place! Awesome picture :D</td>', 'Congrats on 5th place! Awesome picture :D', '2004-10-18 12:48:20.000000', NULL, 0),
